project-root/
├── docs/
│   ├── CLAUDE.md
│   ├── PROJECT_SPECS.md
│   ├── TECH_STACK.md
│   ├── AGENTS.md
│   └── STAGES.md
├── .gitignore
└── README.md


Copy the template for a new project

bash
git clone https://github.com/yourname/claude-webapp-template my-new-app
cd my-new-app
rm -rf .git && git init
Fill in the placeholders – Open each file in docs/ and replace everything in brackets with your app’s details. You can ask Claude to help you generate the initial specs by giving a short description.

Start a Claude Code session

Open the project in VS Code.

In Claude Code, say: “Read all the files in docs/ and acknowledge you understand the project.”

Then: “We are ready to begin Phase 1. Create branch phase-1-foundation and implement the first task from STAGES.md.”

Work phase by phase – After each commit, Claude updates STAGES.md. If your session ends, simply reload the docs and say “Continue from the last completed phase.”

Adapt for a different stack – The template is deliberately generic. If you move away from Cloudflare, just update TECH_STACK.md and adjust the folder structure. The process of context files, phase tracking, and Git branches remains identical.

